WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.520
Welcome to The Explainer.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.120
We're now on step three.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.560
This is exactly where your AI's episodic memory gets built.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.400
And essentially everything you've ever said becomes completely searchable.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.280
Let's walk through what actually happens right on your Mac.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.880
So here's what happens.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.720
The program opens up your export

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.160
and sorts it all out.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.440
Every conversation becomes its own separate entry, and every

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.840
message gets placed right in its proper order.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.400
It also keeps a careful track of who said what.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.400
Your words, the AI's replies, and

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.800
any attachments are all kept apart.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.720
Then it builds an index.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.640
Think of an index as just a really fast

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.880
way to find any word you've ever typed.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.480
And the most important part is

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.240
that nothing is sent anywhere.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.960
The entire process happens locally on this Mac,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.000
and your original file remains completely untouched.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.440
Now you might be wondering why

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.200
does who said what matter?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.480
Well, it's pretty simple.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.960
Something in AI suggested isn't automatically

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.800
something you actually agreed with.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.280
Keeping your personal messages completely separate from

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.760
its replies preserves what actually happened.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.290
So later, when your constitution is being written, it's strictly

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.090
written from your own words and not the AI's.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.970
There is one key thing to be perfectly clear about.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.850
This step fills your episodic memory only.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.410
After it runs, you can search with words you vaguely

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:17.690
remember, maybe a project name or just a phrase, and

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:21.050
every single result points right back to the conversation, allowing

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.130
you to read it in its proper context.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.250
But searchable is not the same as understood.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.290
Your constitution, which is what your AI actually knows about

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.650
you, well, that's a totally separate step that's coming up.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.050
As for how long this takes, it generally

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.370
takes about one to two minutes per gigabyte.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.250
You'll actually see your own estimate right beside this explainer.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.650
Also, if it ever gets interrupted, you don't need to

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.210
worry, it simply picks up right from where it stopped.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.530
Once it's completely done, you'll see exactly

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.770
how many conversations and messages came in.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.610
And we'll run a search together so you can watch

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.170
your AI find something you said a year ago.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.930
Build your searchable history now?

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.210
Press a button below.
